course: dictionary
lesson: 13621
title: Choosing without care
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: The word indiscriminately has parts you can spot. In- means not, discriminate means to choose or tell things apart, and -ly tells you how something is done. So indiscriminately means without choosing carefully, at random or in a careless way.
explain: «The giant swung his club indiscriminately, smashing trees, fences and sheds.» The giant did not pick his targets. He hit whatever was in his way. Ask yourself: is anyone choosing carefully here? No, so the word means carelessly.
explain: «Sam sprayed water indiscriminately, soaking his friends, the dog and the post van.» Sam was not aiming at anything special, and he did not care who got wet. That is the second meaning: without caring who is hurt or affected. «Taking pills indiscriminately, without asking a doctor, can make you very ill.» This is unsafe because it is careless about what you take.
fact: Indiscriminately means without choosing carefully, or at random.
fact: It can also mean without caring who gets hurt or affected.
fact: Indiscriminately is an adverb: it tells you how an action is done, as in «spray indiscriminately».
fact: The opposite idea is choosing carefully, so carefully is close to the opposite of indiscriminately.
fact: Phrases you may meet are «kill indiscriminately», «use indiscriminately» and «spray indiscriminately».
exercise: «The farmer sprayed the field indiscriminately.» What does indiscriminately mean here? | Only at night | *Without care, over everything in the field | Very carefully, one plant at a time | Slowly, with a rake
exercise: Ella says indiscriminately means carefully. What is the mistake? | It means the same as quietly | *It is the opposite: it means without choosing carefully | It means exactly carefully, so she is right | It is only a name for a bird
exercise: The doctor said, «Take your medicine ___, only as the label says.» Which word fits best? | loudly | noisily | *carefully | indiscriminately
test: «The children threw sweets indiscriminately into the crowd.» What does indiscriminately suggest? | Throwing very slowly, one sweet at a time | Throwing with a rule for each child | *Throwing without caring who catches them | Throwing only to the front row
test: The careless giant smashed the glass, the chairs and the door ___. Which word fits best? | Quietly | Sleepily | *Indiscriminately | Politely
exam: Jade says, «Taking pills indiscriminately is safe.» What is the correct answer? | It is safe, as long as you take them quickly | *It is unsafe, because taking them carelessly can harm you | It is safe, because pills always help | It is safe, since doctors never mind
